  "question": {
    "text": "The heats of neutralisation of $\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{COOH}$, $\\mathrm{HCOOH}, \\mathrm{HCN}$ and $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{~S}$ are -13.2,-13.4,-2.9\r\n\r\nand $-3.8 \\mathrm{kCal}$ per equivalent respectively. Arrange the acids in increasing order of acidic strength.",
